                          "log":  [
                                      {
                                          "who":  "josh",
                                          "text":  "This mine area has random lighting throughout with no light source. I\u0027d like you to analyze it and add real light sources throughout in the bright areas, lit by the torches we\u0027ve designed. Also for the torches dont forget that their geometry should also cast shadows.",
                                          "at":  "2026-10-09T04:20:31.0622138Z",
                                          "shot":  "MINEMAZE-1-0.png"
                                      },
                                      {
                                          "who":  "claude",
                                          "text":  "Done: seven real torches now light the mine where the original artists painted their light. I built a tool for it: it reads the brightness of the ORIGINAL art across the whole room (the game\u0027s own pixels, so your future clean textures won\u0027t change it), takes the brightest places at least 240 units apart, finds the nearest wall at each one and mounts a torch there facing into the light pool: 15 units out, about 72 above that floor, with the shader flame. Three are in the big cave (one about 220 units from where you clicked), two on the eastern stretch, and two on the upper level to the south. Each torch\u0027s light casts shadows, and the torch geometry itself is part of what casts them: its stake and cup throw shadows from the other torches and your flashlight. Embers are off, as in the other rooms. If a torch is in an odd spot, click it and say where it should go.",
                                          "at":  "2026-10-09T04:28:14.5286035Z",
                                          "changes":  [
                                                          "rooms\\MINEMAZE.json (new): lights[0..6] seven torches at the original art\u0027s bright places (tools\\Find-PaintedLights.ps1 -Count 7 -Spacing 240), embers off",
