                          "log":  [
                                      {
                                          "who":  "josh",
                                          "text":  "Lets add a torch here as it will backlight the raptor character. As for torches, the shadow of the torch sconce is too \"blobby\" Lets skip the shadow casting of the round part of the torch and try only having the stake porch of the scones cast a shadow.",
                                          "at":  "2026-10-09T13:23:11.2843487Z",
                                          "shot":  "MINEMAZE-4-0.png"
                                      },
                                      {
                                          "who":  "claude",
                                          "text":  "Added torch 5 on that corridor wall, 15 units out and 58 above the floor. The corridor\u0027s ceiling is only 88 up, so it sits a little lower than the 72 I\u0027d normally use, in line with the other mine torches (53-61 up). It gets the bounced lighting and dancing shadows like the rest. The sconce shadow is fixed in two steps: only the wooden stake casts a shadow now (the iron cup, ring, arm and plate and the coals cast none). And a torch never shadows its own sconce: with the light sitting straight above the stake, the stake threw its shadow end-on as a round blob down the wall (a real flame is big enough beside the stake to wash that out). The stake still casts shadows from the other lights and your flashlight. Also: the fog\u0027s light glow only took the first four lights in a room, so a fifth torch would have lit walls but not glowed in the fog. It now takes the four nearest you.",
                                          "at":  "2026-10-09T13:36:20.7827923Z",
                                          "changes":  [
